mac versus pc is one of the oldest  rivalries within the tech industry  windows has dominated this race in terms  of market share and will likely continue  to do so moving forward but i think  apple share of this market is about to  grow substantially over the next decade  now many apple fanboys will claim that  it's about time a given that macs were  always better than pcs but i don't think  that's exactly true  we don't have to look that far back to  see how limiting macs were in the past  for example remember how macbooks only  had usb-c ports or how apple shipped  unreliable butterfly keyboards just to  make the keyboard millimeters thinner or  the time that apple recalled 432  thousand macbook pros because they would  catch on fire clearly macs haven't  always been perfect but ever since apple  ditched intel and released their m1  series of products i think apple's  offerings have become more appealing  than ever before and i'm not the only  one who thinks this either as their  annual growth has far outpaced the pc  market  last year annual sales for pcs grew by  14.6 percent while annual sales for the  mac grew by 28.3  or nearly two times as much  also this growth wasn't just amongst  which americans the laptop market or  liberal college students this statistic  was within the global pc market  considering this i don't think you'd be  surprised to hear that apple hit record  mac revenue numbers pulling in over 10  billion dollars within a single quarter  so here's why mac adoption is going  through the roof and why max market  share may grow as high as the iphone's  market share  likely one of the biggest factors  driving up mac adoption recently is that  apple has become more competitive than  ever before when it comes to value  now this may be a bit confusing as we  see apple continuously churn out  extremely expensive products  after all they do sell a 50 000 pc and a  5 000 monitor but how many people do you  really think buy these products  the top-end mac pro is literally  equivalent to the average american's  annual salary and while you may think  that ripping off customers is apple's  entire business plan if you look deeper  into these products you'll know that  this isn't 100 true given that apple  doesn't even take these products that  seriously one of my favorite tests to do  when it comes to expensive apple  products is to see how long it takes  them to ship it to me today is march 27  2022 and if i order the apple pro stand  right now it'll take until april 8th for  it to arrive or 12 days meanwhile if i  order the mac mini it'll arrive in just  two days or i can pick it up in store  today  now if apple was really trying to sell  the pro stand seriously it wouldn't take  them 12 days to deliver it i'm literally  spending 1 000 on a monitor stand you  would think that they would at least  spend some effort in fast delivery but  they don't because they don't take the  pro stand seriously all these products  that people love to make fun of like the  pro stand apple wheels and the mac pro  are all headline products  while a very small number of people will  actually buy these products and may even  find them valuable the primary purpose  of these products is not to generate  sales but to generate headlines like  this  such headlines serve two purposes which  are building exclusivity and price  anchoring the first purpose needs no  explanation when consumers constantly  see such outrageously priced products  they start to associate apple with  exclusivity and desirability and in  terms of price anchoring when people see  a fifty thousand dollar computer they'll  start to think that a two or three  thousand dollar computer is relatively  not that expensive if we put such  products aside noah we'll see that apple  is extremely competitive in terms of  price and value  for example in terms of desktops the m1  mac mini retails for seven hundred  dollars and you can actually get it for  669 dollars at amazon  gary from the everyday dad thinks that  the mac mini is the best value computer  you can buy on the market  m1 mac mini is literally the best  computer that you can buy for the money  if you disagree i challenge you to  comment down below a desktop computer  that's more portable easy to use and  offers more performance for the same  price as the m1 mac mini if we look at  apple's macbook lineup it's exactly the  same case there as well while the  macbook pros aren't the easiest to  justify for the average person just take  a look at the macbook air it starts at 1  000 which makes it the same price as an  iphone 13 pro and if you're a student  you can actually get it for 900  now again you can find plenty of laptops  for 300 to 500  but when you compare the macbook air to  other laptops that are priced at one  thousand dollars it's extremely  difficult if not impossible to find a  laptop that offers more value per dollar  so while apple still doesn't sell the  super cheap entry-level products the  entry-level products that apple does  sell are basically impossible to beat  thanks to the m1  moving on the second reason that macs  have been doing better than ever before  is their synergy there's of course the  apple ecosystem which is getting harder  and harder to escape by the day but i'm  not even talking about that  rather i'm talking about hardware  synergy  one of the top reasons for the success  of the iphone is that apple is able to  leverage so much more power out of the  same hardware  iphones consistently tend to have less  ram less computing power and less  graphics power than their android  counterparts but despite this in terms  of real world performance iphones often  match if not beat these android  counterparts thanks to their hardware  and software optimization the lack of  such optimization was one of the biggest  shortfalls of the mac but that's no  longer the case of course there's the m1  but that's not the only factor take  apple's unified memory for example  several reports and reviews have  suggested that macs with unified memory  not only match but outperform systems  with twice as much regular ram  also it's not just apple that's  leveraging this optimized hardware some  of the biggest software developers are  finally taking the time to optimize the  software for mac adobe for example  claims that their apps are now 80 faster  on m1 max and looking forward it this  energy should only improve as apple  bridges the gap between their ios  devices and their mac devices  historically it developers have not  wanted to develop software for mac  because it's always been such a niche  market something that's not a niche  market though is the ios app store and  with the introduction of apple silicon  on macs software development for ios and  mac os has basically become identical  according to apple themselves most ios  apps require no modification to run on  apple silicon  now this doesn't mean that supercell is  going to develop clash royale for the  mac but what this does mean though is  that software companies who primarily  deal with windows can leverage the large  base of ios developers to efficiently  port over software to mac so in the  coming years apple will not only have  some of the most value-packed hardware  but some of the most optimized software  and the given that this combination is  what allowed them to perform so well  within the mobile market i'd bet that  it'll play out pretty well within the pc  market as well  while apple's synergy and value are  great if you choose the right products  we can't ignore that mac still have a  few major pitfalls starting with a lack  of repairability and upgradability at  the end of last year apple announced  their self-service repair program which  promised to allow consumers to repair  their own iphones and macs with genuine  apple parts but with the recent release  of the mac studio it's not clear how  true apple will stay to this promise  if you guys haven't heard yet if you  crack open the mac studio you'll  actually find that the storage device is  removable and replaceable however what  luke miani found was that if you switch  the slot in which the storage device is  placed or swap the storage device with  another storage device with a different  capacity the mac studio refuses to boot  clearly there's some sort of software  log and or encryption that prevents  users from changing the storage which is  quite stupid i have no idea why apple  doesn't just let people swap the storage  because here's the thing i bet 95  percent of apple customers won't want to  take apart a brand new computer and try  to upgrade the storage so even if apple  allowed this option it these guys would  just pay apple for the extra storage  anyway so it's not like apple would lose  out on much revenue in the meantime they  can avoid all the criticism they receive  regarding lack of repair ability the  second biggest shortfall of max is sort  of related to the first point which is  their base storage options while the mac  mini and macbook air offer great value  in terms of performance they don't offer  great value in terms of storage these  machines should offer a minimum of 512  gigabytes of storage and their higher  end mac studios and macbook pro should  offer a minimum of one terabyte of  storage their current storage sizes are  unacceptable in 2022 aside from lack of  repairability and underwhelming starting  storage the last biggest complaint  regarding macs is their limited software  if you want to play games for example  there's still no reason to get a mac and  i don't think this will change anytime  soon similarly some high-end software  like the autodesk suite have yet to  really be refined for apple silicon  however unlike gaming i think this can  improve in the imminent future as  software companies leverage ios  developers but we'll just have to wait  and see  while macs do still have some shortfalls  i don't think the shortfalls will  actually sway the average consumer that  much like i said the average consumer  won't want to open up their computer  anyway so a lack of repairability slash  upgradability isn't that big of a deal  though it would be nice if apple allowed  for this  and in terms of software limitations  most people will mainly just spend their  time doing work and browsing through  social media and unless you're an  architect or a 3d designer or something  the software limitations wouldn't even  apply to you something else to note is  that all of these issues are relatively  easy to fix  it's not that hard for apple to bump up  the starting storage or light knob on  the software restrictions that prevent  upgrades recently apple has been a lot  more open to feedback given that they  brought back sd card slots hdmi ports  and regular usb ports so hopefully  they'll make these changes as well if  they do make these changes i think mac  adoption will only accelerate moving  forward especially with the launch of  the m2 chip now i don't think mac will  ever become the dominant pc operating  system and just like ios will probably  never become the dominant mobile  operating system however i do think  apple can grow their pc market share  closer to their mobile market share  right now macs only account for about 10  of the global pc market while ios  accounts for 28 of the global mobile  market  due to all the reasons outlined so far  in this video i think it's quite  possible that over the next decade  apple's market share in the pc market  grows closer to 20  this is quite odd for me to say actually  because i've always been a massive fan  of windows due to the versatility and  customizability the first videos on this  youtube channel are actually videos of  me building my pc and discussing the gpu  market it was until recently that i got  my first mac and while i now have the  option of using either windows or mac i  honestly don't think i'll be using my  windows computer that much moving  forward because the mac can do  everything i need but better faster and  smoother and as more people give the m1  a shot i think they'll come to the same  conclusion but that's just what i think  are you guys team windows or team meg  comment that down below also drop a like  if you think apple killed it with the m1  and of course consider checking out our  international channels to watch our  videos in other languages and consider  subscribing and see more questions  logically answered but until then i'm  hari and i'll see you guys on the next  one
 

